.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt NOHUP 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm nohup
.Nd run a command immune to hangups
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
executes
.Ar command
with the caller's environment.
The kernel queues signals and the exec'd child does not install a SIGHUP
handler, so a queued hangup does not terminate it.
.Pp
The runtime has no stdout descriptor or
.Fn isatty
path, so
.Nm
implements the non-terminal case: it does not redirect output.
The POSIX terminal-only
.Pa nohup.out
redirect needs a stdout/fd API and is a documented follow-up.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A command that cannot be found exits 127; a command that cannot be executed
exits 126.
A usage error exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr env 1 ,
.Xr kill 1
.Sh STANDARDS
IEEE Std 1003.1-2024
.Pq POSIX.1-2024 ,
except the unavailable terminal-only output redirect noted above.
